n with a commanding financial position, having raised more than $12 million and holding $6.6 million on hand, while Republican nominee Doug Ollivant, a veteran and national security analyst, has raised roughly $250,000. Minor-party and independent candidates on the ballot appear non-competitive.\n\nExpert raters broadly place the race in the Likely Democratic column, with several calling it Safe or Solid Democratic, and prediction markets price Vindman's chances near 94 percent. With no public general-election polling available, the outlook rests on fundamentals, which point to a comfortable but not insurmountable Democratic advantage in a midterm environment where affordability and data-center growth are prominent local issues.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.972, "margin": 13.04}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9562, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9664, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9683, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9585, "margin": 12.0}]}